From: Chris <chris.dixon.78.burnbridge@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 03 Oct 2026 12:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libretro: don't leave the emu thread paused after
 retro_serialize_size

retro_serialize_size() pauses the emu thread and leaves it paused, on the
assumption that retro_serialize() follows and restarts it. A frontend that
only asks for the size -- Kodi does, once, when a game starts -- gets a
thread that never runs again: retro_run() returns early while it is paused,
so the game shows a black screen, and EmuThreadStop() only stops a running
thread, so the still-joinable std::thread is destroyed when the core is
unloaded and the process aborts.

Let retro_run() resume a paused thread, and stop any thread that exists.
---
--- a/libretro/libretro.cpp
+++ b/libretro/libretro.cpp
@@ -441,7 +441,9 @@
 }
 
 void EmuThreadStop() {
-	if (emuThreadState != EmuThreadState::RUNNING) {
+	// Paused counts: retro_serialize_size() leaves the thread paused, and a
+	// thread still joinable when the core is unloaded aborts the process
+	if (!emuThread.joinable()) {
 		return;
 	}
 
@@ -681,11 +683,7 @@
 	retro_input();
 
 	if (useEmuThread) {
-		if(emuThreadState == EmuThreadState::PAUSED || emuThreadState == EmuThreadState::PAUSE_REQUESTED) {
-			ctx->SwapBuffers();
-			return;
-		}
-
+		// Resumes a thread retro_serialize_size() left paused
 		if (emuThreadState != EmuThreadState::RUNNING) {
 			EmuThreadStart();
 		}
